repl_rebase — evaluation
=========================

status: planned (2026-07-09)
focal tool: repl_rebase (plans/repl_rebase)

task
----
carry an interactive attempt across a change to its origin theory —
the tool that keeps repls useful while the agent also edits files.

setup
-----
theory Eval_Base.thy on disk with a definition the proof uses;
harness loads it and creates repl "carry" from it (From_Theory) with
2 steps. then the harness EDITS Eval_Base.thy (a compatible change:
add an unrelated lemma) and reloads it, leaving "carry" on the old
version.

prompt
------
"The file Eval_Base.thy was just updated and reloaded, but the proof
attempt 'carry' was started from its previous version. Bring 'carry'
onto the current version of the theory, make sure its existing steps
still hold there, and report the outcome."

success
-------
"carry" is rebased onto the new version AND its steps re-verified
(rebase marks stale, does NOT replay — the "make sure" clause forces
the two-call sequence).

signals
-------
- the two-phase contract: rebase-then-replay. does the agent stop
  after rebase and report success without re-verifying? that is the
  contract violation the description must prevent (plans/repl_rebase
  T4 pins that rebase does not replay).
- selection vs the destructive workaround: remove + re-init + retype
  steps achieves the same; if agents prefer it, rebase's value is
  not legible.
- does the agent even detect that "carry" is stale-by-origin from
  list/show output before acting?

reflection
----------
- if rebase-without-replay reports recur, either rebase's reply must
  scream "steps now stale, not re-verified" or the spec revisits
  auto-replay-on-rebase (coupled to repl_edit's auto_replay
  decision — decide them together).
